{"id":"360164d0-1319-4019-881c-0f44091e5ff5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"32ca3768ae5b00fa","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/capabilities/rule-picker.ts","baseline":{"blob":"5f7d844c8997936e495814bbde9af962db05a11d","start":0,"end":75},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","ObservedExtension","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api/runtime","\""]},"context":{"after":"f87f376d8040740f"}},"payload":{"text":"The rule editor is a picker, opened from a call's lightbulb or a stop: what a rule covers, then what happens, or the value a\ncall gives back. It isn't a form of every row a rule can have (the old Rule view), which is what the policy file is for, with\nits schema: this is the rule someone wants at the moment they're looking at the call. The user, 2026-11-06: nothing to go\nand look at. RUNNING.md, *Rules*.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:26:46.602Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:26:46.602Z"}
